From: Hans Wennborg <hans@chromium.org>
Date: Wed, 25 Oct 2017 01:30:52 -0700
Subject: XML_ErrorString: handle XML_ERROR_INVALID_ARGUMENT

Previously, this enum didn't have any error string.

Origin: https://github.com/libexpat/libexpat/commit/5ae72360c66629509684297abf78e8a62894c252
---
 lib/xmlparse.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/lib/xmlparse.c b/lib/xmlparse.c
index 8ccd031..48410f3 100644
--- a/lib/xmlparse.c
+++ b/lib/xmlparse.c
@@ -2215,7 +2215,8 @@ XML_ErrorString(enum XML_Error code)
     XML_L("cannot suspend in external parameter entity"),
     XML_L("reserved prefix (xml) must not be undeclared or bound to another namespace name"),
     XML_L("reserved prefix (xmlns) must not be declared or undeclared"),
-    XML_L("prefix must not be bound to one of the reserved namespace names")
+    XML_L("prefix must not be bound to one of the reserved namespace names"),
+    XML_L("invalid argument")
   };
   if (code > 0 && code < sizeof(message)/sizeof(message[0]))
     return message[code];
